{"type":"finding","severity":"trivial","fileName":"src/state/reviewer-adapters.ts","codegenInstructions":"Verify each finding against current code. Fix only still-valid issues, skip the rest with a brief reason, keep changes minimal, and validate.\n\nIn @src/state/reviewer-adapters.ts around lines 168 - 176, The current validation for reviewer.evidence_path (variable evidencePath in the validation block) allows the bare prefix \"docs/work/\" to pass; update the check so that if evidencePath startsWith(\"docs/work/\") it must also contain at least one non-empty path segment after that prefix (e.g. ensure evidencePath.length > \"docs/work/\".length and the substring after the prefix does not start with empty/another slash), or alternatively require a filename or extension via a simple regex (for example enforce /^docs\\/work\\/[^\\/]+\\/.+$/ or /^docs\\/work\\/.+\\.[^\\/]+$/) before throwing the existing Error; adjust the conditional around the startsWith(\"docs/work/\") branch accordingly so bare \"docs/work/\" is rejected.","suggestions":[]}
{"type":"finding","severity":"trivial","fileName":"src/state/reviewer-adapters.ts","codegenInstructions":"Verify each finding against current code. Fix only still-valid issues, skip the rest with a brief reason, keep changes minimal, and validate.\n\nIn @src/state/reviewer-adapters.ts around lines 104 - 112, The function validateTypedReviewerAdapter currently lets reviewers with empty/whitespace reviewer.type pass through unvalidated, creating a fail-open path; rename validateTypedReviewerAdapter to tryValidateReviewerAdapter (or add explicit JSDoc) to signal partial validation, and update its declaration and all callers to use the new name (or update docs) so callers know it may return the original ReviewerAdapterInput when type is empty; ensure the signature still references ReviewerAdapterInput & { type: ReviewerAdapterType | \"\" } and add a short comment above tryValidateReviewerAdapter describing that it performs full validation via validateReviewerAdapter only when reviewer.type is a non-empty string and otherwise returns the input unchanged.","suggestions":[]}
