{"type":"finding","severity":"major","fileName":"test/landing-gates.test.mjs","codegenInstructions":"Verify each finding against current code. Fix only still-valid issues, skip the rest with a brief reason, keep changes minimal, and validate.\n\nIn @test/landing-gates.test.mjs around lines 861 - 909, The tests added under land-check (test names \"land-check validates human review replacement evidence before landing\" and \"land-check accepts current human review evidence without model-review claims\") lack coverage for blocker and stale-human-review scenarios: add two new tests—one that uses writeHumanReviewEvidence to create a human review with reviewer_verdict set to \"blocker\" and asserts runBandit([... \"land-check\", \"<ID>\"]) returns non-zero and reports blocking the safe-to-land verdict, and another that writes human review evidence with source_drift_status indicating \"stale\" (or with a mismatched sourceHead) and asserts land-check fails for stale evidence; to support this make writeHumanReviewEvidence accept explicit overrides for reviewer_verdict and source_drift_status (or sourceHead) so tests can inject \"blocker\" and \"stale\" cases; update assertions to check stderr/stdout messages for blockage/stale evidence accordingly and mirror the same changes for the other similar test sites noted in the review.","suggestions":[]}
